Package: cepip
Type: Package
Title: Cell Explanatory Power with Inflection Point (CEP-IP) and CMRF
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Kah Keng", "Wong", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "kahkeng3@gmail.com",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-7359-6202"))
Description: Implements the CEP-IP framework for single-cell co-expression
    analysis. A generalized additive model (GAM) fitted by REML with a
    penalized residual sum of squares (PRSS) search over the basis dimension
    relates a gene of interest to the mean of its partner genes. Cells are
    ranked by their explanatory power, and the inflection point is the first
    negative-to-positive zero crossing of a residual GAM. Optional extensions
    are the Spearman-Kendall cell-level score (SKCS) and copula-based module
    refinement with fold cross-validation (CMRF), which recovers cells near
    the module through a tolerance band and a repeated stratified k-fold
    cross-validation gate. Downstream helpers give per-donor module
    fractions, paired donor-level differential expression and donor-level
    association models. CEP-IP is described in Wong (2026)
    <doi:10.1016/j.cmpb.2026.109372>.
